<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 2: Self-proposed rubrics are effective rewards in non-verifiable domains.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 3: RL with self-proposed rubrics (CaT-RL) is better than SFT.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 4: CaT produces better reference estimates than single-sample and selection baselines.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px5" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 5: CaT scales with the number of rollouts <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px6" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 6: CaT reasons about prior rollouts rather than acting as another rollout.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px7" title="In 4.1 Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Compute as Teacher: Turning InferenceCompute Into Reference-Free Supervision" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Result 7: CaT reconciles rather than selects to disagree with consensus.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
